<section class="result-section">
    <h2>Animated memes</h2>

    <div class="result-text-content">
        <p class="why-jstmemit-text-block">
            <b>Turn any existing message into a meme</b>
            After adding Jstmemit, right-click a message, click on "Apps", choose Jstmemit and select the meme you want to
            get. This way you can remake any existing (even voice!) message into a quote, a fake news report or a Grok tweet.
        </p>
        <p class="why-jstmemit-text-block">
            <b>Generate voice messages with /voice</b>
            Use /voice to narrate your text using one of 23 different voices. Perfect for making soundboard phrases or simply
            narrating funny messages. And it's free, same as all other features.
        </p>
    </div>
    <img
        class="result-meme"
        src="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1524494877490942152/1543371239366725772/meme.webp?ex=6aa277b9&is=6aa12639&hm=98e6a83ec9aed8eb201286bbf6d739ed57c6e57339be8bb5e8f5c550f54503fb&"
        alt="Meme with a photo of a minecraft base and 'our base is trash' text over it"
    />
</section>

<style>
    .result-section {
        position: relative;
        margin-top: 5.5rem;
        display: flex;
        align-items: stretch;
        gap: 2rem;
    }

    .result-section img {
        width: 50%;
        border-radius: 2rem;
        border: 2px solid var(--color-bubblegum-pink);
    }

    .result-section h3 {
        font-weight: 700;
        margin-block-start: 0;
        margin-block-end: 0.5em;
    }

    .result-text-content {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        min-height: 100%;
    }

    .why-jstmemit-text-block {
        padding: 0 2rem;
        border-radius: 2rem;
    }

    h2 {
        right: 2rem;
    }

    @media screen and (max-width: 768px) {
        .result-section {
            flex-direction: column-reverse;
        }

        .result-section img {
            width: 100%;
        }
    }
</style>
